    //                            SCHEDULING
    // ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    //
    // Memory layout recap:
    //   - C_param(j, i): Buffer C has shape (n, n) with dimension 0 (j)
    //     contiguous in memory. So for fixed i, scanning j is unit-stride.
    //   - A_param(k, i): Buffer A has shape (m, n) with dimension 0 (k)
    //     contiguous in memory. For fixed (i, j), scanning k is unit-stride
    //     for both A[i, k] and A[j, k], which is ideal for vectorized
    //     reductions over k.
