    C_param.set(C);
    A_param.set(A);

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Schedule
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //
    // Data layout:
    //   - C(j, i): j is the fastest-varying dimension (row-major w.r.t. C[i][j]),
    //     so sweeping j is unit-stride in memory.
    //   - A(k, i): k is the fastest-varying dimension, so for fixed (i, j),
    //     the reduction over k walks A[i][k] and A[j][k] contiguously.
    //
    // We:
    //   * Tile (i, j) for cache locality on C.
    //   * Tile k for reuse of A and C tiles.
    //   * Parallelize across tiles of i (independent row blocks).
    //   * Vectorize across j (stride-1).
    //   * Lightly unroll the inner k chunk to improve ILP.
    //

